WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:05.200
Where to start knitting?

2
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:08.220
If you have cards that were pre-punched

3
00:00:08.250 --> 00:00:13.340
specifically for your machine,
and the card has a line printed,

4
00:00:13.370 --> 00:00:18.960
you simply need to line up up
the line and start knitting.

5
00:00:19.360 --> 00:00:25.580
But cards from different
manufacturers don't always line up.

6
00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:29.180
Think about this. The punch card mechanism

7
00:00:29.210 --> 00:00:33.380
itself lives inside the body
of your knitting machine.

8
00:00:33.410 --> 00:00:36.540
And the different brands and models have

9
00:00:36.570 --> 00:00:43.800
different mechanisms and they have unique
positions within the machine bed itself.

10
00:00:45.160 --> 00:00:48.820
I like to imagine little fingers that are

11
00:00:48.850 --> 00:00:53.660
inside the mechanism that read
the holes of the card.

12
00:00:53.680 --> 00:00:56.220
Now, the fingers in one machine may be

13
00:00:56.250 --> 00:01:01.860
positioned an inch down from the top edge
of the card reader and the fingers

14
00:01:01.890 --> 00:01:07.880
in another machine may be half inch down
from the top edge of the card reader.

15
00:01:08.320 --> 00:01:12.540
If you insert the same card in two
different machines

16
00:01:12.570 --> 00:01:18.850
and line up the pre-printed line,
the fingers might be reading a different

17
00:01:18.880 --> 00:01:26.320
row and the first row that knits will
be different on the two machines.

18
00:01:26.440 --> 00:01:28.780
Now sure, there are some rules out there

19
00:01:28.810 --> 00:01:35.700
about Silver Singer versus Brother and
there may be color coding on the cards.

20
00:01:35.730 --> 00:01:42.020
But more importantly, you need
to understand that there is a difference.

21
00:01:42.050 --> 00:01:44.820
You might have mystery cards and you don't

22
00:01:44.850 --> 00:01:47.340
know if they were designed
for your machine.

23
00:01:47.370 --> 00:01:49.680
You may have inherited some cards

24
00:01:49.710 --> 00:01:54.290
that were punched by a knitter and they
don't have any color or any indication

25
00:01:54.320 --> 00:01:58.700
on them of what machine
they were designed for.

26
00:01:58.730 --> 00:02:01.490
The best way to find out what the

27
00:02:01.520 --> 00:02:06.040
first rows of your card on your
machine is, is to try it.

